# FOR control variable after the loop. Implementation-defined: ed.3
# 7.3.3.4.2 (ed.2 2.6.5.2) states that the value of the control variable
# after the loop terminates is implementation-dependent (and that it shall
# not be modified inside the loop; for_bound_modified covers the bound).
# sum is defined and checked; i_after records what IronPLC does: the
# control variable holds the first value that failed the test (n + 1), and
# with n < 1 the loop body never runs and i holds the initial value 1.
period_ms: 100
program: main
inputs: n
outputs: i_after sum
status: implementation-defined
reference: IEC 61131-3 ed.3 7.3.3.4.2 (FOR statement)
---
0 n=3  => i_after=4 sum=6
1 n=0  => i_after=1 sum=0
2 n=1  => i_after=2 sum=1
3 n=-2 => i_after=1 sum=0
